# Example ReRDMFT input file: carbon monoxide (R = 1.128 Angstrom), cc-pVDZ basis, GNOF (3 coupling subspaces of
# 2 orbitals), 4-component with the MIN-MAX stage (FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG), NEO and CHOLESKY TRUE.
# Same first stage as co_ccpvdz_c4_gnof_neo_cholesky.inp (no-pair minimization over the 56 positive-energy
# spinors, -113.0044414 Ha). FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE then continues from that minimum with rotations that also
# mix the 20 occupied positive-energy spinors (occupation > 1e-6) with the 60 negative-energy ones: NEO converges the
# orbitals to the saddle point of order 1200 (energy maximized along those electron-positron directions, minimized
# along the rest), alternating with the full re-minimization of the occupation numbers. The stage needs the
# negative-energy block of the MO Cholesky vectors too, built separately. Measured: ~8 min in total (~4 min for the
# first stage, ~2 min for the min-max stage, 2 macro-iterations), the min-max stage moves the energy by 1.5e-9 Ha.
# The check of the saddle type (dense diagonalization of the Hessian and count of its negative eigenvalues)
# runs only with DEBUG TRUE; at this size it would need the dense two-electron tensor (~4 GB) and was not run.
# Follow the run with `tail -f co_ccpvdz_c4_gnof_neg_neo_cholesky.live`.
NELEC 14
BASIS co-cc-pvdz.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
SCF_DIRECT_4C FALSE  # preserve this example's pre-existing SCF path (SCF_DIRECT_4C now defaults TRUE for plain C4_SPINOR runs)
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 3
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE
ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO
CHOLESKY TRUE
ON_DEMAND_ERI FALSE  # off here to keep this example's historical fast runtime (the whole packed AO tensor already fits in memory); default is TRUE, see lih_gnof_c4_full_optimization_cholesky.inp for the on-demand path demonstrated explicitly.

GEOMETRY
C   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
O   0.000000   0.000000   1.128000
END
